				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody">Dimento awoke the day after the battle, still feeling the flush of victory.  Never shall the mistress of the plane of nightmare again plague his dreams or his waking hours, that hold had been broken.
<br />

<br />
As he set about to forage the day's breakfast and prepare of an adventure in the catacombs of Lesser Fay, six figures wearing the mark of the Wudan guild surrounded him.
<br />

<br />
"It's war you know," said the tallest of the figures.
<br />

<br />
"What?" Asked Dimento.
<br />

<br />
"It's war!  The last straw has been broken, you have stolen our prey for the last time!" Dimento had to replay that last sentance in his mind as it came across in such a whine as to make it almost unintelligable.
<br />

<br />
"There was a first time?  What are you people talking about?  Get out of my way, I gots things to do and vile creatures to incinerate."
<br />

<br />
"You're going to die NOW!" and with that the 6 figures attacked.
<br />

<br />
Dimento decided at this point he should really pay attention to these people.  For the most part, Wudan and Fusion did not cross paths all that often.  Fusion a guild for the independant somewhat anti-social minded of Norrath,  had yet to enter the higher realms.
<br />

<br />
Examining his foes he could see that they had acquired armor, items, and weapons with powerfull enchantments, perhaps more powerfull than his own, and the skills displayed and used by his attackers would indicate that they had advanced abilities at least equalling his own.
<br />

<br />
Six on one, not a smart fight, he could hear magic incantations, the unsheathing of swords, and the twanging of bows all at once.  There was no way this battle could be won.  Dimento quickly called out to Tunare, and Tunare the Blessed Mother, answered and sent Dimento to a safer area of Butcherblock mountains.
<br />

<br />
Quickly he opened his much used spell book and memorized the spell to send himself to the Nexus.
<br />

<br />
His only offensive move, was to shout, "You're morons, but hey!  I will be quite happy to oblige, when the match is more even!"
<br />

<br />
Arriving at the Nexus ring, he quickly made his way through the crowds to the agreed upon 'meeting place' by the Bazaar.  There he found one of his guild's more powerfull members Gamorfy, the Barbarian Warrior there with High Elf Cleric, Welsh as well as his wife the beautiful  Wood Elf Rogue, Leeha.
<br />

<br />
"Hello Gamorfy, it seems trouble has found us again."
<br />

<br />
Gamorfy sighed, "Yes afraid so.  What do you think we should do about it?  They say they're going to war us for 24 days."
<br />

<br />
"24 days?  That's it?  They way they'd complained about whatever it is that they are upset about you'd think we'd be under permanent seige."  Dimento said, around a mouthfull of fruit he's always seemingly able to forage out of nothing.
<br />

<br />
Leeha was amazed at her husband, while he had helped her with her foraging skills to the point that she might not starve, he was always foraging rabit meat in the middle of the ocean, or foraging fruits and vegatables in the middle of a stone work room.  How he does it, she'll never know and is almost afraid to ask.
<br />

<br />
"What'd we do anyway?"
<br />

<br />
Again Gamorfy sighs, "Apparently their upset that we went to the Plane of Nightmare and killed Terris Thule with Coventant of the Wolf, and those other guilds."
<br />

<br />
Dimento paused, obviously confused, "That's it?  One of our members didn't draw a giant sized picture of Raveena being molested by a troll, or worse &lt;shudder&gt; a dwarf?"
<br />

<br />
Gamorfy chuckled, "Afraid so.  What do you want to do about it?"
<br />

<br />
"Hmm...  Man, I figured we'd done something serious.  I'm suprised they care all that much.  Must be Ascending Dawn beat them to Tallon Zek again or something, I guess they need us to take some frustration out on."
<br />

<br />
"Perhaps, again, what do we do?"
<br />

<br />
Dimento chuckles, "Why accomodate them, of course!  This will be fun, and I'm sure they're in for quite a shock when they see how well we know how to war."
<br />

<br />
And so it began...  Fusion and Covenant of the Wolf began a week of war with Wudan, giving as well as they received, suprising Wudan such that the war as ended not in 24 days, but in only 8.<div style="vertical-align: bottom"><br /><br /><br />_________________<br /><img src="http://home.comcast.net/~robertminneman/Dimento-DFRTTGDM.jpg" border="0" /></div></span><span class="gensmall"></span></td>
